Explain the commant: "git reset"
Git reset command is a powerful and versatile command in  git that is used to undo changes in your repository

git reset [mode] [commit]

Types of options:
> soft (it reset the HEAD to the specified commit but leaves the staging index and working directory unchanged)

git reset --soft HEAD~1

> mixed (Rests the "HEAD: to the specified commit and rests the staging area to match that commit but does not change the working directory)

git reset HEAD~1

> Hard
mode rests the HEAD the staging area and the working directory to the specified commit

git reset --Hard HEAD~1
